<p><%= report[:samples] %> samples · <%= report[:labelled] %> labelled · <%= report[:compared] %> compared. Excluded: <%= report[:disputed] %> disputed, <%= report[:uncertain] %> uncertain, <%= report[:abstained] %> abstained and <%= report[:unpredicted] %> without a usable prediction.</p>
<p>“Fail” is positive: false positives flag good support; false negatives miss bad support. Counts use the latest label per expert. Disputed or uncertain samples cannot supply ground truth.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Failure detection confusion matrix</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Prediction</th><th scope="col">Expert fail</th><th scope="col">Expert pass</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Fail</th><td><%= report[:true_positive] %> true positives</td><td><%= report[:false_positive] %> false positives</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Pass</th><td><%= report[:false_negative] %> false negatives</td><td><%= report[:true_negative] %> true negatives</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<dl class="source-metadata"><% { precision: "Failure precision", recall: "Failure recall", disagreement_rate: "Machine / expert disagreement", inter_rater_agreement: "Pairwise expert agreement" }.each do |key, name| %><dt><%= name %></dt><dd><%= report[key].nil? ? "Not enough evidence" : number_to_percentage(report[key] * 100, precision: 1) %></dd><% end %></dl>
<p class="muted-copy">Pairwise agreement uses <%= report[:pairs] %> pairs of certain expert labels; it is not chance-corrected. A small or selected sample does not prove accuracy across the company corpus. Do not tune on held-out samples.</p>
